      "title": "Letterboxd review of Seven Samurai",
      "snippet": "[Letterboxd Review of \"Seven Samurai\"] The astonishing thing about Seven Samurai is that it seems far too modern for a film made sixty years ago. As much as I love black-and-white films, it is hard to deny that some films, no matter how good they are, begin to seem antiquated when compared with modern films in their genre.But Seven Samurai can still compete with action films today. Perhaps its length and the amount of time spent on characterization and story may put off some of the audience, but the film's grip on viewers is undeniable. You can't stop watching it until the end.The cinematography plays no small part in creating an a",
